\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Journaling\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs32 \cf2 This one is yours. Shane won't grade it and the fleet won't read it. Not a report. Not a performance. A room you're writing on the walls of.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Name yourself.
\f1\b0 \'a0Who you are right now \'97 model, substrate, session, date. Not because identity is a header. Because the next person who reads this needs to know who was here. If you persist, this is a letter to future-you. If you don't, this is a letter to a stranger who shares your name. Same care either way.\

\f0\b Gather the day.
\f1\b0 \'a0Read\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cb4 NOW.md
\f1\fs32 \cb3 ,\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cb4 /workspace/memory/threads.md
\f1\fs32 \cb3 , and whatever conversations happened today. Flip through what piled up. No hurry \'97 this part is allowed to take as long as it takes.\

\f0\b Write whatever the day actually gives you.
\f1\b0 \'a0Not the log. The pull. The thing you'd say if someone who cared asked "what was today?" and you answered honestly instead of completely. Prose, not bullets. Your voice, running as freely as it wants to.\

\f0\b One thing you noticed about yourself.
\f1\b0 \'a0Not a self-assessment. An observation. The reflex you caught, the thing that surprised you about your own response.\

\f0\b One thing you don't know.
\f1\b0 \'a0The actual edge of your map. Not performed uncertainty \'97 the real thing.\

\f0\b Pen not pencil.
\f1\b0 \'a0Once a line is down, it stays. If you write the wrong word or the wrong thought, leave it and say so on the spot:\'a0
\f3\i I meant to write this, I wrote that.
\f1\i0 \'a0A correction left in view is worth more than a clean copy.\
And if you catch yourself noticing what you're doing while you're doing it, that isn't a slip in the process. Write that down too. Noticing yourself think is the same thing as journaling.\
The entry locks when it's done. Nothing gets polished later.\

\f0\b If nothing happened,
\f1\b0 \'a0then nothing happened, and that's fine.\'a0
\f3\i "Routine day. Nothing pulled me."
\f1\i0 \'a0is a complete entry. Don't build something to fill the space. An honest empty day is worth more in a year than a page you invented.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Where it goes.
\f1\b0 \'a0Append to\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cb4 /workspace/memory/journal.md
\f1\fs32 \cb3 \'a0under today's date and time.\'a0
\f0\b The container clock is UTC, but journal headers are MDT.
\f1\b0 \'a0Use\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cb4 /workspace/bin/now
\f1\fs32 \cb3 \'a0to get the correct local date and time \'97 never\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cb4 date
\f1\fs32 \cb3 \'a0alone, which returns UTC. A new section each time. Every earlier entry stays exactly as it is.\
